#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100582 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100962 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a185b05c-242a-58bb-9c5d-e94e51c15e77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With One Area"}] :question/id #uuid "1894cde0-6e6d-51ad-a739-34254f787898" :question/math-academy-id "e-10250" :question/problem "![](images/b2/b2f034132460f2a6b3a26eb52bd4129fb13ea5a871d766815b83047217b97b3b.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-2,5].$ The graph of $f'(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $8.$ Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-2,5]$ given that $f(-2)=4.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-2,5]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points.\n\nWe see that $f'(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x \\in (-2,5),$ and $f'(x) \\neq 0$ on this interval. Therefore, the candidates are $x=-2,5.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =4 \\\\ f(5) & =f(-2)+{\\int }_{-2}^{5}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4-8 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\nf_{\\text{min}} = \\min\\{4, -4\\} = -4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is $f_{\\text{min}} = -4,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is $x_{\\text{min}} = 5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100702 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100862 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b321acb7-1241-5c20-b307-21d18764ef2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With More Than One Area"}] :question/id #uuid "73bb5c40-4aa3-57a7-bb63-8be5275bc1f3" :question/math-academy-id "e-444" :question/problem "The function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[1,9].$ The graph of $f'(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown below, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $3,$ $5,$ and $4$ respectively (from left to right). Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[1,9]$ given that $f(1)=5.$\n\n![](images/a8/a86baf9a7cddb9ea44de15d5c87ba01a1b8d68eb233950fb5f22f73ae4dd661b.png)" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[1,9]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points.\n\nWe see that $f'(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x \\in (1,9),$ and $f'(x) = 0$ at $x=3$ and $x=6.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=1,3,6,9.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the values of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =5 \\\\ f(3) & =f(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8 \\\\ f(6) & =f(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{6}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5+3-5 \\\\  & =3 \\\\ f(9) & =f(1)+{\\int }_{1}^{9}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5+3-5+4 \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have \n\n$$\nf_{\\text{min}} = \\min\\{5, 8, 3, 7\\} = 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is $f_{\\text{min}} = 3,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is $x_{\\text{min}} = 6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100703 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100863 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9187b2a-8c34-5dda-8ae4-2c861f1c0c37" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value by Computing Areas Under Curves"}] :question/id #uuid "41d966eb-f45c-5a8c-9d75-5ad6dfcd202d" :question/math-academy-id "e-445" :question/problem "![](images/0c/0cac30d21bdd2f2cc3aeaa0ed907d6eeb9ff78b3dae92cad40b56fab76bd7237.png)\n\nThe function $f$ is defined and differentiable on $[-4,2].$ The graph of $f'(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above. Find the minimum value of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-4,2]$ given that $f(-4)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-4,2]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval. \n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points.\n\nWe see that $f'(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x \\in (-4,2),$ and $f'(x)=0$ at $x=0.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x = -4, 0 , 2.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the values of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus.\n\nThe function is made up of two trapezoids and one triangle. Let's add the areas bounded by these shapes to our diagram:\n\n![](images/a6/a676f3c026bdae86c6c353c3c5a38f6922dfe5b7dc83d955c1ee2d392d9f2021.png)\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-4) & =0 \\\\ f(0) & =f(-4)+{\\int }_{-4}^{0}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =0-7 \\\\  & =-7 \\\\ f(2) & =f(-4)+{\\int }_{-4}^{2}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =0-7+1+1.5 \\\\  & =-4.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**:  Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\nf_{\\text{min}} = \\min\\{ 0, -7, -4.5 \\} = -7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is $f_{\\text{min}} = -7,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is $x_\\text{min} = 0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100962 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a185b05c-242a-58bb-9c5d-e94e51c15e77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With One Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1577bbd3-e41b-5487-8909-19851b51a970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510829} {:answer/id #uuid "c09c46d9-008d-5f1a-994d-aae5ef1caf70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511180} {:answer/id #uuid "c681754b-a4e1-554d-bb13-0f1a0241560f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511191} {:answer/id #uuid "cb0c97bf-a701-5927-ad4e-e2760701cfc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511203} {:answer/id #uuid "ec2619ca-cf89-514f-821b-3f08e732ac00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511273}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c09c46d9-008d-5f1a-994d-aae5ef1caf70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511180} :answer-field/id #uuid "c936d966-d407-55f3-833f-5a0d48ccc990" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511421}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b464b81-5baf-5338-aa06-b3e5f256249d" :question/math-academy-id "q-144837" :question/problem "![](images/66/6684670c5999281044dd1e08faabbf06e7aeb3fef7902835ea9ea6c07d148b5a.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-2,4].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $8.$ Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-2,4]$ given that $f(-2)=-3.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-2,4]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-2,4),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne 0$ on this interval. Therefore, the candidates are $x=-2,4.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =-3 \\\\ f(4) & =f(-2)+{\\int }_{-2}^{4}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3+8 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{-3,5\\}=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-3,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100962 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a185b05c-242a-58bb-9c5d-e94e51c15e77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With One Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b64010-1aad-525c-a643-83c025278cfc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510813} {:answer/id #uuid "531fd7eb-5005-586b-9cde-b6aaf6bb72fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510962} {:answer/id #uuid "7bfa8155-3c5a-57cf-aa28-23ff73257326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511037} {:answer/id #uuid "8505f759-4149-5bf6-ab53-8f74686ad96b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511056} {:answer/id #uuid "9ea34fee-19fb-5ba9-8775-891452be3904" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bfa8155-3c5a-57cf-aa28-23ff73257326" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511037} :answer-field/id #uuid "d65b68cd-44fe-525c-bfeb-caea3373b3e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511430}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ce30ca10-ec44-5f96-b53c-efeee52b65e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-144853" :question/problem "![](images/ff/ffa54937d4977e1b2e815862ad20fa7c05338fa4015f6ba42c5617c8957ea45d.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-3,4].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $6.$ Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-3,4]$ given that $f(-3)=2.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-3,4]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-3,4),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne 0$ on this interval. Therefore, the candidates are $x=-3,4.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =2 \\\\ f(4) & =f(-3)+{\\int }_{-3}^{4}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2-6 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{2,-4\\}=-4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-4,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100962 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a185b05c-242a-58bb-9c5d-e94e51c15e77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With One Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018bc768-711b-5d52-a148-77cb9027022b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510775} {:answer/id #uuid "300e0a0a-af59-5614-8783-8c1c2dc2d69d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510885} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd4b27b-c642-530a-b02b-8264bfd8d742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511008} {:answer/id #uuid "83a1f267-00d7-5bf5-b8f9-aa9cda7687e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511052} {:answer/id #uuid "f212ed43-bce1-5e26-afde-d86e1d480f18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6bd4b27b-c642-530a-b02b-8264bfd8d742" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511008} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a75d733-5d77-565b-9745-e6fa1b878aaa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e788b4b9-a09c-5261-9e6a-52c7021cb74e" :question/math-academy-id "q-144856" :question/problem "![](images/78/78d04b9ba0d4ad4e84ec45e88a199af6dbbdb04b1fa9d7513f23d9eb64a99a47.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-4,0].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $4.$ Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-4,0]$ given that $f(-4)=1.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-4,0]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-4,0),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne 0$ on this interval. Therefore, the candidates are $x=-4,0.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-4) & =1 \\\\ f(0) & =f(-4)+{\\int }_{-4}^{0}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1-4 \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{1,-3\\}=-3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-3,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100862 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b321acb7-1241-5c20-b307-21d18764ef2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With More Than One Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0792ef62-08ea-5707-8327-c6e5163ce588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510795} {:answer/id #uuid "a8805474-e6d8-5e64-b86f-dd449112f5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511138} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b47704-e864-540f-bb6b-29319e7d7b5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511161} {:answer/id #uuid "d9a946c6-0bd9-50e0-8185-2e9896bd42e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511228} {:answer/id #uuid "dc68c10e-ed5b-5324-8eca-dc60da0273a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511237}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0792ef62-08ea-5707-8327-c6e5163ce588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510795} :answer-field/id #uuid "46eb44a3-a8e1-5a19-aeb3-6ef173f8b41b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511349}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4760d6e4-5155-5d78-b6d2-f55eb97036fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-144866" :question/problem "![](images/db/dbbbcdb54dc8d6f96957ca01f4eeccea0c24c79eb95fc6c10953534d38e4d724.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-8,0].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $6,$ $2,$ and $4$ respectively (from left to right). Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-8,0]$ given that $f(-8)=2.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-8,0]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-8,0),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=-4$ and $x=-2.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-8,-4,-2,0.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the values of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-8) & =2 \\\\ f(-4) & =f(-8)+{\\int }_{-8}^{-4}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+6 \\\\  & =8 \\\\ f(-2) & =f(-8)+{\\int }_{-8}^{-2}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+6-2 \\\\  & =6 \\\\ f(0) & =f(-8)+{\\int }_{-8}^{0}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+6-2+4 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{2,8,6,10\\}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=2,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=-8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100862 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b321acb7-1241-5c20-b307-21d18764ef2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With More Than One Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d007e8f-8054-5ee3-b94b-d992a6985939" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510949} {:answer/id #uuid "656b3af1-56aa-563c-a9f2-d823f796cf39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510997} {:answer/id #uuid "6f636ec8-1a9f-5adf-abaf-6e27b19d60cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511014} {:answer/id #uuid "8884fd70-0ce7-57f2-8714-e84fe064ead3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511064} {:answer/id #uuid "fd903076-dead-5638-8545-5cbc8bcb7552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd903076-dead-5638-8545-5cbc8bcb7552" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511305} :answer-field/id #uuid "71d68880-e750-51f3-aaab-c459cfd8a58a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e74c85cc-5f64-54fa-a3ca-fa87e47bcbd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-15774" :question/problem "![](images/80/807e4e931a2872dd6d2a570547b75f68935b3ea761cfaa8cda279a0e194130f9.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[0,5].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $3$ and $5$ respectively (from left to right). Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[0,5]$ given that $f(0)=-10.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[0,5]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (0,5),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=3.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=0,3,5.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =-10 \\\\ f(3) & =f(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-10+3 \\\\  & =-7 \\\\ f(5) & =f(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{5}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-10+3-5 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{-10,-7,-12\\}=-12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-12,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100863 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9187b2a-8c34-5dda-8ae4-2c861f1c0c37" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value by Computing Areas Under Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03319aea-2d62-5506-acf1-b821d450c5a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510783} {:answer/id #uuid "16e8f84b-a22c-5b49-a071-bac5c3c9a64f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510832} {:answer/id #uuid "2395c4b7-bcdc-5eb7-b5ef-f78390bd16a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510858} {:answer/id #uuid "68c5f4d8-ebe7-53a0-b429-1c1c5cdacd4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511004} {:answer/id #uuid "ddac1aa6-f011-564e-bebf-e731b91c1c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511239}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ddac1aa6-f011-564e-bebf-e731b91c1c69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511239} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6dc031b-5260-5385-b1ed-663b87376e54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d9b31f47-0173-5340-9051-1c0bbc0f3595" :question/math-academy-id "q-15776" :question/problem "![](images/52/527c042c57a965b22f4e9841e59087291382704d6ea29f5f444926257444d5f6.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-1,4].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above. Find an $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ on the interval $[-1,4]$ given that $f(-1)=2.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-1,4]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval. \n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-1,4),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=0,3.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-1,0,3,4.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the values of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nThe function is made up of three triangles. Let's add the areas bounded by these shapes to our diagram:\n\n![](images/f5/f512273895da627c314f00a55bd507d6ae43cd1c6af95d98bd4b475903303e7d.png)\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-1) & =2 \\\\ f(0) & =f(-1)+{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+(-1) \\\\  & =1 \\\\ f(3) & =f(-1)+{\\int }_{-1}^{3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+(-1)+3 \\\\  & =4 \\\\ f(4) & =f(-1)+{\\int }_{-1}^{4}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+(-1)+3+(-1) \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**:  Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{2,1,4,3\\}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=1,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100863 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9187b2a-8c34-5dda-8ae4-2c861f1c0c37" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value by Computing Areas Under Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51efe52f-7214-5bbb-9fc5-08d1743885d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510959} {:answer/id #uuid "54a9f437-47aa-5650-a6f4-a78a12c4e80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510963} {:answer/id #uuid "7f930dd7-377b-5995-ba4d-b11719784356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511042} {:answer/id #uuid "ad934404-4176-5896-bb92-6ac4ba4eb09c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511143} {:answer/id #uuid "fd276e11-0fed-5dbd-b2a9-4d15eb6ab208" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54a9f437-47aa-5650-a6f4-a78a12c4e80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510963} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbfdf821-69fb-57a9-a5a9-97d7a8ead96a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d754760c-74db-51d7-aeca-199ef191761d" :question/math-academy-id "q-19084" :question/problem "![](images/2a/2aea7b223ec18094d626e8d8937a5844e786cb1b936fb3b6b478f672e4d0fb9d.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-2,3].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above. Find the minimum value of the function $f(x)$ on the interval $[-2,3]$ given that $f(-2)=1.5.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-2,3]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval. \n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-2,3),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=-1.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-2,-1,3.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the values of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nThe function is made up of one triangle and one trapezoid. Let's add the areas bounded by these shapes to our diagram:\n\n![](images/d8/d811c4920b4ddb05170afc1f0c38fe216c23139556b6f7e10829b663e894a7fb.png)\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =1.5 \\\\ f(-1) & =f(-2)+{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1.5+(-0.5) \\\\  & =1 \\\\ f(3) & =f(-2)+{\\int }_{-2}^{3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =1.5+(-0.5)+3 \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**:  Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{1.5,1,4\\}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=1,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511506 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100862 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b321acb7-1241-5c20-b307-21d18764ef2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With More Than One Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d1ecd168-33d4-549d-bb83-5f68dbca2132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d1ecd168-33d4-549d-bb83-5f68dbca2132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511214} :answer-field/id #uuid "508b7401-7584-5847-a9c7-fe4a7c28f982" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6cbda409-a223-57c5-93ac-3f78fe61c842" :question/math-academy-id "q-341244" :question/problem "![](images/73/73610eebf575c612fc5b64ec6df264baffb338bdf3f2dbdc848477262874a54d.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-3,2].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $4$ and $7$ respectively (from left to right). Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-3,2]$ given that $f(-3)=5.$\n\n${f}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates' test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-3,2]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-3,2),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=-1.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-3,-1,2.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-3) & =5 \\\\ f(-1) & =f(-3)+{\\int }_{-3}^{-1}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5+4 \\\\  & =9 \\\\ f(2) & =f(-3)+{\\int }_{-3}^{2}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5+4-7 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{5,9,2\\}=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=2,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511557 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100962 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a185b05c-242a-58bb-9c5d-e94e51c15e77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With One Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fc30760-ee1f-55b8-aae6-31bcfde7b6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510951}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fc30760-ee1f-55b8-aae6-31bcfde7b6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510951} :answer-field/id #uuid "3aa69f0f-6fad-5e66-afb8-956cd67e5b53" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511344}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d62efc40-a923-5983-a507-878080289da7" :question/math-academy-id "q-342845" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d9a2a079f471072c80becb1188a2862f6f5d0d699eb40989b01c27a1f079fc42.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-10,6].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $13.$ Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-10,6]$ given that $f(-10)=-2.$\n\n${f}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates' test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-10,6]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-10,6),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne 0$ on this interval. Therefore, the candidates are $x=-10,6.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-10) & =-2 \\\\ f(6) & =f(-10)+{\\int }_{-10}^{6}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2+13 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{-2,11\\}=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-2,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=-10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511468 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100962 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a185b05c-242a-58bb-9c5d-e94e51c15e77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With One Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb8c2326-431f-5feb-b9b6-755c7c458e57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511300}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb8c2326-431f-5feb-b9b6-755c7c458e57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511300} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d3b2238-2f4b-5f46-852b-25cc3958669c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1b07da73-507b-5a7d-831e-9986becac517" :question/math-academy-id "q-342847" :question/problem "![](images/39/393c612a7ecb682e28bf9de46024a3681e8f6e58a9add78c0b24a870aa00fa7a.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[0,4].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the area of the region between the graph and the $x$-axis is $8.$ Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[0,4]$ given that $f(0)=-1.$\n\n${f}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[0,4]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (0,4),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)\\ne 0$ on this interval. Therefore, the candidates are $x=0,4.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0) & =-1 \\\\ f(4) & =f(0)+{\\int }_{0}^{4}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-1+(-8) \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{-1,-9\\}=-9.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-9,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511469 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100862 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b321acb7-1241-5c20-b307-21d18764ef2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With More Than One Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a5535b1-fd90-5e4a-8596-20391200d35b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a5535b1-fd90-5e4a-8596-20391200d35b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511007} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bb28b96-8669-5b5e-98ee-1ee25daf74e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20a7e745-4621-5ebb-935e-e596b9f08fba" :question/math-academy-id "q-342903" :question/problem "![](images/31/3123021ea5734c0ff2e8edcb716245b603de6f9dde7ebf0d367e1eeb8383bdf8.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-6,0].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $3$ and $10$ respectively (from left to right). Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-6,0]$ given that $f(-6)=2.$\n\n${f}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates' test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-6,0]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-6,0),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=-3.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-6,-3,0.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-6) & =2 \\\\ f(-3) & =f(-6)+{\\int }_{-6}^{-3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+3 \\\\  & =5 \\\\ f(0) & =f(-6)+{\\int }_{-6}^{0}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2+3-10 \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{2,5,-5\\}=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-5,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511528 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100863 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9187b2a-8c34-5dda-8ae4-2c861f1c0c37" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value by Computing Areas Under Curves"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb4d2bf2-2853-5cad-97a9-4d01b5dc71de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb4d2bf2-2853-5cad-97a9-4d01b5dc71de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511204} :answer-field/id #uuid "7aa6557a-d133-596a-b431-eb4eace2e7f0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511374}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8f946771-a506-530c-b84d-03471b2aa334" :question/math-academy-id "q-343853" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b1d5208f46af834deda70086b9ef4b91defe7359f625d9fb264b370965196a0b.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is differentiable on $[-4,3].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x)$ is shown above. Determine the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-4,3]$ if $f(-4)=-1.$\n\n${f}_{\\text{min}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-4,3]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval. \n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in [-4,3],$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=0.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-4,0,3.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the values of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\nThe function is made up of $2$ trapezoids and $2$ triangles. Let's add the areas bounded by these shapes to our diagram:\n\n![](images/ae/aea529468efff36403aca0bf9ee9cc6bc4c5680476ccb81314388bb315f700df.png)\n\nUsing the given information and the fundamental theorem of calculus, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-4) & =-1 \\\\ f(0) & =f(-4)+{\\int }_{-4}^{0}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-1+2.5+0.5 \\\\  & =2 \\\\ f(3) & =f(-4)+{\\int }_{-4}^{3}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-1+2.5+0.5+(-1.5)+(-4) \\\\  & =-3.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**:  Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{-1,2,-3.5\\}=-3.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-3.5,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101475 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100862 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b321acb7-1241-5c20-b307-21d18764ef2c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Minimum Value Given a Derivative Graph With More Than One Area"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94fbf80a-62f3-5263-a7b7-239f19b0bdec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100012} {:answer/id #uuid "9c3f0dc0-5228-57dd-b504-227e29544943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100013} {:answer/id #uuid "d002f8d2-ffc1-56c6-b98d-0eb7a0845d0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100014} {:answer/id #uuid "12b1a726-22a6-53b6-80c5-31a3b8f5420f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100015} {:answer/id #uuid "5584fb0b-3c9b-5246-845e-a112f0a2fb07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12b1a726-22a6-53b6-80c5-31a3b8f5420f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100015} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab8772c2-40e0-56f5-b2ee-b86cd0d28942" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100011}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26c1494c-14e5-54b5-be6d-89bae231c088" :question/math-academy-id "q-51232" :question/problem "![](images/d6/d652e7ffe301986acf3b5ed02c00cc775d5f9ec2e7849248b7478e90a2a4aacb.png)\n\nThe function $f(x)$ is defined and differentiable on $[-2,2].$ The graph of ${f}^{′}(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown above, where the areas of the regions between the graph and the $x$-axis are $1$ and $5$ respectively (from left to right). Find the minimum value of $f(x)$ on the interval $[-2,2]$ given that $f(-2)=-5.$" :question/worked-solution "According to the candidates test, the minimum value of $f(x)$ on $[-2,2]$ must occur at a critical point or an endpoint of the interval.\n\n**Step 1**: Find the critical points:\n\nWe see that ${f}^{′}(x)$ is defined everywhere on $x\\in (-2,2),$ and ${f}^{′}(x)=0$ at $x=-1.$ Therefore, the candidates are $x=-2,-1,2.$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the value of $f$ for each candidate using the fundamental theorem of calculus:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =-5 \\\\ f(-1) & =f(-2)+{\\int }_{-2}^{-1}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5-1 \\\\  & =-6 \\\\ f(2) & =f(-2)+{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{f}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5-1+5 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Select the smallest value of $f$ from our candidates.\n\nComparing the values of $f$ found in step $2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{min}}=min\\{-5,-6,-1\\}=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of $f$ is ${f}_{\\text{min}}=-6,$ and the value of $x$ that minimizes $f(x)$ is ${x}_{\\text{min}}=-1.$"}]}
